// The `markup` namespace (area 19, "Text formats"). Each operation is
// listed, typed, in `jadpo-std`'s operation table, which names the Rust
// function in `jadpo-value` that runs it; a test holds these stubs to that
// table. Neither fails: every text is CommonMark, and every `Html` was made
// safe when it was built.

public library markup {
    /// `markdown` rendered as CommonMark (0.31.2), then made safe as every
    /// `Html` is: raw HTML inside it is kept only where the sanitiser keeps
    /// it, and an image is shown as its description, since `Html` keeps no
    /// images.
    function to_html(markdown: Markdown) -> Html {}

    /// The text people read in `html`: each block (a paragraph, a heading,
    /// a list item, a quote, a code block) on its own line, `<br>` a line
    /// break, white space run together as a browser shows it, kept as
    /// written in a code block.
    function to_plain_text(html: Html) -> Text {}
}
